- For "aaa", the distinct non-empty subsequences are: "a", "aa", "aaa" -> 3.
- For "abc", the distinct non-empty subsequences are: "a", "b", "c", "ab", "ac", "bc", "abc" -> 7.

Constraints:
- The input string consists of lowercase English letters.
- The length of the string can be up to 10^5.
- The result must be returned modulo 10^9+7.

